# Section 6, BEAM: the steps of tools/figs/FIG46.jou (figure 46) on /null -- CassWithExitPupil.in on a
# 64-point grid, the intensity at element 1 (the obscuration plane, an entrance pupil: the intensity there IS
# the beam profile) with the default UNIFORM beam, then a GAUSSIAN of waist radius 1.0 in x and y.  The
# Gaussian is normalized to the uniform flux (2026-10-19): its sum is the uniform sum less the truncated tail.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in s06b
cd $TMP/s06b
old CassWithExitPupil.in
pgd
/null
mod ngridpts=64
q
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_beam_uniform
int 1
# TRANSCRIPT: s06_beam_gauss
beam
gau
1.0
1.0
int 1
# TRANSCRIPT-OFF
# EXPECT: Enter beam type \(UNIFORM, GAUSSIAN, COS\*\*POWER, DIPOLE\): \[UNIFORM\]: gau
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 3\.3322\d*D-04;[^\n]*\s+Sum of intensity= 9\.0636\d*D-01
# EXPECT: Peak intensity= 1\.5947\d*D-03;[^\n]*\s+Sum of intensity= 5\.7778\d*D-01
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
